east/up/north -> [ 0, 1, 0 ] (expect [0, 1, 0])
east/up/above -> [ 0, 0, 1 ] (expect [0, 0, 1])
east/north/above -> [ 0, -1, 0 ] (expect [0, -1, 0])

=== Worked example, heading (4D) ===
Setup: A facing is fixed when stated, and so is where the head points. Left and right are judged from both.
Premises:
  Bell is east, south, above and same time relative to Ash.
  Cole is west, same latitude, above and later relative to Ash.
  Fay is west, south, same height and same time relative to Cole.
  Eve is west, north, below and earlier relative to Cole.
  Cole is west, south, same height and same time relative to Dell.
  Cole faces Dell.
  Cole's head points toward Ash.
Claim:    Bell is on Cole's left.   ->  TRUE
  f = Dell-Cole = [1,1,0]   h = Ash-Cole = [1,0,-1]   v = Bell-Cole = [2,-1,0]  (east, north, up)
  det[h,f,v] = 3 -> left; body signs ahead/left/above = [1, 1, 1]
  lure flat (today's facing rung, plane only): right
  lure head-up (head assumed to point above):  right

planar lure must be wrong: 2000 items from 2073 layouts; float solver agrees 2000/2000; mean usable quadruples per layout 158.0; flat lure right 0%, head-up lure right 0%
no lure required: 2000 items from 2073 layouts; float solver agrees 2000/2000; mean usable quadruples per layout 258.1; flat lure right 37%, head-up lure right 37%
